    13	## Global constraints
    14	
    15	- **On the owner's Mac: unit tests and bounded tiny checks only.** A "tiny check" means a tiny model, ≤ 2 environments, ≤ 2 updates, < 1 GB RAM and < 2 min. Anything larger runs on the pod. (W:ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/plan.md:21, quoted.) Only Claude operates the pod. No training/GPU/build work is needed to write these briefs.
    16	- Deployment resource fit is 128 envs/rank, two ranks, 64 vCPU total. Choose `native_threads` by measurement, with `2*native_threads + other workers <= 64`; component speed does not establish complete-update speed (W:ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/plan.md:26).
    17	- Preserve Isaiah's Rust/PyO3 caller-owned storage and canonical `scripts/run_ppo.py`. No v2 model/collector/trainer, C ABI or ctypes. Never change vendored kernel bytes, including module declarations.
    18	- Stateless observation-only policy: no recurrent/temporal state, history tokens or opponent identity in actor/critic inputs, rewards, losses, normalization or selection. Grammar prefix state resets each observation. Diagnostic full snapshots never enter model input.
    19	- Fail explicitly; no silent fallback/coercion, Python grammar or dynamic `getattr` dispatch. Follow I0–I12 and L1/L2/L3/L4/L6/L7 (W:ops/rebuild-2026-09-29/plan.md:79,100).
    20	- Future builds: `CARGO_BUILD_JOBS=2 CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true UV_OFFLINE=true`. Invoke just on this Mac as `uvx --offline --from rust-just just`. This base has no `reference` extra. Missing offline dependencies block that check; do not silently fetch.
    21	- Only these two briefs change now. Future docs/cookbook updates below belong to implementation. Codex does not commit, push, merge, switch branches or touch another worktree.
