   512	
   513	`terminal_metrics` lazily creates fresh dict/arrays; banks/margin preserve f64, episode_steps is i64-checked Python int, winner integer, econ arrays C-contiguous `[32]` int64. Return None before a terminal transition, after a nonterminal step, or for a selected explicit reset. Never expose mutable native record storage. Seed/snapshot consumers are rollback/seed tests, run provenance and Task 3.3; full terminal snapshots are not required here. Task 7.3 uses codec plus seeded replay.
   514	
   515	
   516	## Trainer consumption and L6 contract
   517	
   518	| Observed W behavior | Required owner/action |
   519	|---|---|
   520	| W:python/owl/rl.py:329,339–377 allocates pinned tensors and retained NumPy views; :379,644,772 returns reused buffers | 1.5 keeps this pattern: one caller-owned buffer set (Claude review R1). Kaggriculture pinning failure is explicit; Orbit's existing fallback stays unchanged. |
   521	| W:python/owl/train/ppo.py:561 enables nonblocking only on CUDA+pinned; :564 transfers the initial reset observation | Covered by the entry fence of the next env call. No trainer change. |
   522	| :870–878 policy forward then env.step; :882–889 rewards/dones H2D; :896–907 stores prior obs/actions/current transition; :912–916 copies new obs | All reads are enqueued on the current stream before the next `env.step`; the adapter's entry fence waits for them. Rollout write_step copies at :486–503 are device-side. |
   523	| :2273–2281 actions-to-CPU is blocking by default; :2296–2301 uses that default. No Event/explicit reuse fence in ppo.py | That blocking transfer already drains the stream, so the fence costs ~nothing today, but the fence, not this incidental sync, is the contract. If a future change makes the action copy nonblocking, the fence still holds. |
   524	| :2242–2250 CPU observation transfer clones; :882–889 CPU rewards/dones `.to(cpu)` may alias | CPU training: `rewards[idx] = 0.0` at :987 writes into the env's rewards buffer. Harmless (next call overwrites it), but 3.1 clones CPU rewards/dones before artificial truncation edits so native transition bytes keep their meaning for diagnostics. |
   525	| :975–985 bootstraps from the pre-reset subset (`_obs_index` makes an unpinned copy); :987 zeros rewards; :988 sets dones; :991 ignores truncate's returned batch | In-place truncate keeps :991 correct unchanged: the reset rows land in the same buffers that `next_obs` refers to, and :912–916 copies them afterwards. 3.2 preserves the Kaggriculture economic reward (L2) instead of :987's zeroing, keeping Orbit behavior. |
   526	| :270–464 storage hardcodes Orbit dims; :2057–2098 mask/action maps are Orbit-only; :2106 field mapper is partly generic | 3.1 adds Kaggriculture storage/typed mappings; no adapter reshapes into Orbit's four slots. |
   527	| W:scripts/run_ppo.py:154–161 constructs rollout env directly; :1281–1289 constructs eval env; :1365 accumulates shaped return, :1372 gets terminal metrics, :1380 uses return for result; :1582–1590 eval copies are nonblocking on CUDA | 3.1 routes both through the factory (passing `transfer_device`); 3.2 uses raw terminal banks/winner; 3.3 supplies the evaluation seed function. The eval env gets the same entry fence. |
